ADDITIONAL NOTICE ON LAWFUL USE

All personal data produced by this software is randomly synthesized fictional
information. It does not correspond to any real person, address, or account.
Card numbers use publicly documented test BIN ranges and, while they pass the
Luhn checksum, they are not valid payment instruments.

This software is intended solely for:

  1. Developers testing form validation and signup flows of their OWN products.
  2. UI demonstrations and educational examples in non-production contexts.
  3. Seeding test databases and performing boundary/stress testing.

It is strictly prohibited to use this software for:

  1. Registering accounts on real platforms (Amazon, Stripe, banks, etc.).
  2. Passing KYC verification or conducting any financial transaction.
  3. Circumventing platform policies, fraud, or any unlawful activity.

Using fictitious identity data for real financial operations constitutes fraud
and violates the criminal law of many jurisdictions. Users are solely
responsible for complying with all applicable laws in their jurisdiction.
